      "where": "/museum/network-onchain · default · 1440x1000 · en-US",
      "evidence": "evidence/judge-visual-index-filter-empty.png",
      "observation": "Typing \"zzzzq\" in Filter by title shows \"0 of 169 shown\" and \"Nothing matches this filter.\" while the Accessions group (3 links) stays listed above it. With \"cent\" the Accessions and Media references groups also stay.",
      "consequence": "The count and message say nothing matched while records are still shown, so the filter looks broken and visitors cannot trust what it hides.",
      "change": "Apply the title filter to every group (accessions, media references, object records) or state which groups are not filtered; the count must equal the visible links.",
      "acceptance_check": "For a query that matches nothing, no entity link is visible besides the Nothing matches message; for \"cent\" the count equals the number of visible links.",
      "admission": "baseline",
      "reopen_reason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V-002",
      "targets": ["J03", "J05"],
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "where": "/museum/network-onchain · works grid · 1440x1000 · en-US",
      "evidence": "evidence/index-1440x1000-03.png",
      "observation": "Seven works without an image render as full-size grey tiles reading \"No published image\", the same size as the artworks, in two rows at the end of the grid.",
      "consequence": "A quarter of the grid is blank boxes that look like failed loads, and they pull the eye from the verified artworks.",
      "change": "Move the seven works to a compact text list under the grid with one sentence that they are presented through live generators, or render them as small text-only cards.",
      "acceptance_check": "The works grid contains only image cards; works without images are listed as text no taller than one line each, at all three viewports.",
      "admission": "baseline",
      "reopen_reason": null
    },
