      "observation": "Every card is still a fixed square (283 px at 1440, 220 at 820, 131 at 390) with dark bands above and below landscape images and at the sides of portrait ones; the six-image landscape row in Works in the collection shows each photograph at about 283x190.",
      "consequence": "Photographs read as boxed thumbnails and, at 390 px, as two ~131 px images, so detail is hard to judge. This is the one remaining gap to 8.5 on J06.",
      "change": "Let the image frame follow the verified image proportion (aspect-ratio from the manifest dimensions, aligned to the top of the row), or at least drop the grey fill so bands do not read as part of the work; use one column below 480 px.",
